module System

### Marker protocol for the types an `Unbroken[T]` can hold.
###
### A type obeys `UnbrokenType` when it lowers to a byte-or-larger machine integer that the hardware
### can load, store, and read-modify-write in one step without a lock: the fixed-width integers
### `S8`..`S64` and `U8`..`U64`. `S128`/`U128` are left out (not every target changes 128 bits in
### one step without a lock), and so is `Bool`, whose `i1` lowering is smaller than a byte.
###
### It has no required routines. It exists only to constrain `Unbroken[T]` (`needs T obeys UnbrokenType`),
### so any other `T` is a build error.
### :see: {Unbroken}
protocol UnbrokenType
